<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Former smoker: smoked cigarettes heavily for about 25 years, about 40 pack-years by his estimate, and quit about 30 years ago through a cessation program; no tobacco, vaping, or cannabis since; no alcohol; no other drug use [S]</item><item>Actor and director, now working part time on photography, writing, and voice projects; married and lives with his spouse in a single-story home [S]</item><item>Walks about 10 minutes at a time around the house and garden; uses a wheelchair for long distances such as airports [S]</item><item>No occupational dust or fume exposure; no biomass or wood-stove exposure; no pets [S]</item><item>Supports: spouse, adult children, long-time friends and colleagues; wants to use his experience to persuade smokers to quit [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

